<!-- ══════════════════════════════ AUDIT ══════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap stack gap-8">
    <div class="stack gap-3">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 — Where we are</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.65rem;">The homepage is still the 2020 Docusaurus scaffold</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Two buttons, three emoji paragraphs, one static PNG — about 130 lines total. Everything that would
        make a visitor install has to be found somewhere else.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat"><span class="n">130</span><span class="l">lines in the entire homepage</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="n">11</span><span class="l">top-level sidebar entries, all emoji-prefixed</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="n warn">28,093<span style="font-size:0.6em">px</span></span><span class="l">height of the themes page — 124 PNGs, 8&nbsp;MB, no filter</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="n warn">0</span><span class="l">segment reference pages showing what the segment looks like</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="n">117</span><span class="l">segments, reachable only by guessing a category</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="n warn">3</span><span class="l">clicks minimum from homepage to an install command</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="stack gap-4">
      <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem;">Concrete defects found in the codebase</h3>
      <div class="findings">
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev block">Blocking</span>
          <p><b>“Get Started →” lands on a theory page.</b> <code>configuration/introduction.mdx</code> carries <code>slug: /</code>, so the primary homepage CTA opens an essay about blocks and segments — not an install command. The sidebar’s actual first item is Getting&nbsp;Started&nbsp;›&nbsp;Installation&nbsp;›&nbsp;Windows, which the CTA never reaches.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev block">Blocking</span>
          <p><b>No index pages exist.</b> Getting Started, Segments, and all eight segment sub-groups are bare categories — clicking them only expands a tree. <code>static/llms.txt</code> already links <code>/docs/segments/overview</code> and <code>/docs/configuration/overview</code>; neither page exists, and <code>onBrokenLinks: 'ignore'</code> hides it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev block">Blocking</span>
          <p><b>Segment discovery depends on guessing a bucket.</b> <code>kubectl</code>, <code>helm</code> and <code>argocd</code> live under CLI, not Cloud. <code>docker</code> is CLI. <code>winget</code> is System. Every group is <code>collapsed: true</code> by default, so the default view of 117 segments shows nothing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev friction">Friction</span>
          <p><b>The theme gallery is one 124-image scroll.</b> No search, no tags, no filter, no per-theme URL, no way to apply one. The Nerd-Font requirement is a sentence of prose, not a facet. It is also one of only two homepage CTAs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev friction">Friction</span>
          <p><b>The FAQ absorbs everything with no home.</b> 24 headings covering PowerShell, fonts, Windows Terminal, JetBrains, Conda, venv, Zsh, Fish, Xonsh, Vim and posh-git. There is no troubleshooting section, no per-shell page and no per-terminal page.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev friction">Friction</span>
          <p><b>Orphan and near-orphan docs.</b> <code>docs/auth.mdx</code> is in no sidebar — only reachable via an OAuth redirect. <code>Advanced</code> is a category with exactly one child. <code>dsc</code>, <code>themes</code>, <code>share</code>, <code>faq</code>, <code>migrating</code> and <code>contributors</code> float loose at root.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev friction">Friction</span>
          <p><b>Navbar priorities are inverted.</b> Sponsor and Swag sit in primary left nav beside Docs and Blog, above a non-closeable sponsor bar. The blog has averaged under one post a year since 2022. Themes and Segments — the two things people actually come for — are not in the nav at all.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="finding">
          <span class="sev polish">Polish</span>
          <p><b>The CSS has hash-coupled selectors.</b> <code>a.getStarted_Sjon</code> and <code>.themedImage_ToTc</code> target generated CSS-module hashes and break silently on upgrade. <code>--ifm-color-primary-lightest</code> is <code>rgb(8,9,10)</code> — near-black. <code>--ifm-font-family-monospace</code> is set to <code>"Inter"</code>. Fira Code is fetched from Google Fonts and never referenced.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ FIELD ══════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap stack gap-8">
    <div class="stack gap-3">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 — What the field does now</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.65rem;">Four idioms, and Starship shares our worst habit</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Twelve sites measured directly, not recalled. The dominant patterns are consistent enough to treat
        as a checklist — and the single closest competitor fails the same test we do.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tbl-scroll">
      <table class="t">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Site</th><th>Hero</th><th>Nav</th><th>Reference at scale</th><th style="text-align:right;">Read</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>starship.rs</td>
            <td>Logo only. No screenshot of the prompt.</td>
            <td>One item: Configuration.</td>
            <td>~100 modules on one page + right TOC.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict down">same trap</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>atuin.sh</td>
            <td>Animated terminal built in DOM. Buttons read <code>$ get-started</code>.</td>
            <td>History · AI · Blog · Docs.</td>
            <td>Docs on a subdomain, kept small.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict up">closest model</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>bun.com</td>
            <td>Install box <em>is</em> the hero. Version in the button.</td>
            <td>Docs · Reference · Guides split.</td>
            <td>Generated reference as its own searchable app.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict up">steal the split</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>zed.dev</td>
            <td>Product chrome re-rendered in DOM, real diagnostics as text.</td>
            <td>Extensions · Docs · Business · Pricing.</td>
            <td>Pushes settings into an in-app editor.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict up">type as brand</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>tauri.app</td>
            <td>Nine-way package-manager tabbed install widget.</td>
            <td>Guides · References split.</td>
            <td>Card grid + platform facet + <code>Ctrl-K</code>.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict up">best filter</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>biomejs.dev</td>
            <td>Logo, then a real rendered diagnostic block.</td>
            <td>Docs · Playground · Blog.</td>
            <td>511 rules split language × 9 groups, badge column.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict up">best taxonomy</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>ray.so/themes</td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td>Live DOM previews, <code>/{author}/{theme}</code> URLs, one-click apply.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict up">gallery model</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>ghostty.org</td>
            <td>Client-rendered — served an empty <code>&lt;main&gt;</code> to a real browser.</td>
            <td>Docs · Discord · GitHub · Download.</td>
            <td>Hundreds of options on one page; docs admit it is unfit.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict down">avoid</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>docs.astral.sh</td>
            <td>Docs <em>are</em> the homepage. Benchmark charts above the fold.</td>
            <td>Material sidebar.</td>
            <td>900 rules in ~50 tables, lifecycle badges, no filter.</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict up">badge column</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>warp.dev</td>
            <td>Interactive configurator panel.</td>
            <td>Enterprise mega-menu.</td>
            <td>—</td>
            <td style="text-align:right;"><span class="verdict down">nav drift</span></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="stack gap-4">
      <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem;">The four idioms</h3>
      <div class="findings">
        <div class="finding"><span class="sev polish">Idiom 1</span><p><b>The hero is the install command.</b> Bun, Atuin, Astro and Tauri all put a copyable command above the fold, with an OS or package-manager toggle and the current version in the button. Nobody makes you click through.</p></div>
        <div class="finding"><span class="sev polish">Idiom 2</span><p><b>Product surfaces are rendered in the DOM, never screenshotted.</b> Crisp at any DPI, selectable, theme-reactive, diffable in git, indexable. PNG galleries now read as dated — which is exactly what our themes page is.</p></div>
        <div class="finding"><span class="sev polish">Idiom 3</span><p><b>Dark-first, but zoned.</b> One flat black is out. Warp tints section washes purple/blue/green/amber over a near-black ground; Atuin runs <code>#0f1722</code> with a green and warm-cream pair. Calibrated neutral ramps plus one saturated accent — no gradient mesh, no glass, no grain.</p></div>
        <div class="finding"><span class="sev polish">Idiom 4</span><p><b>Typography carries the brand.</b> Zed self-hosts four families; Ghostty picked Pretendard; Atuin pairs DM Sans with Space Mono. The sites that read as templates are the ones on stock Inter over a stock generator theme — Starship and Oh My Posh, both.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout">
        <b>Free win, one line:</b> Starship prepends <code>"Nerd Font"</code> to its monospace stack, so Nerd Font glyphs render correctly in code blocks for anyone who has the font installed. Every powerline character in our docs currently falls back to tofu for visitors without it.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════ IA ══════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap stack gap-8">
    <div class="stack gap-3">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 — Navigation architecture</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:1.65rem;">Three structures, increasing ambition</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The current sidebar mixes categories and loose pages at the same level, hides its largest surface
        behind a collapsed node, and has no landing page anywhere. Each option below fixes strictly more
        than the last.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ia-grid">

      <!-- IA-1 -->
      <article class="ia">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">IA-1</p>
          <h3>Tidy</h3>
          <p class="small">Same shape, defects removed. No new pages beyond three indexes. Ships in a day.</p>
        </header>
<pre class="tree"><b>Nav</b>  Docs · Themes · Blog · ⌘K · GitHub

<b>Docs</b>
├─ <i>Overview</i>            <s>new hub page at /docs</s>
├─ Getting started
│  ├─ <i>Overview</i>
│  ├─ Install ▸ Windows / macOS / Linux
│  ├─ Nerd Fonts
│  ├─ Set up your shell
│  ├─ Pick a theme
│  └─ Upgrade
├─ Configuration
│  ├─ Concepts            <s>was “Introduction”</s>
│  ├─ General · Blocks · Segments
│  ├─ Colors · Templates · Data
│  ├─ Transient · Secondary · Debug
│  └─ Tooltips · Streaming · Title
├─ Segments
│  ├─ <i>All segments (117)</i>   <s>new index</s>
│  └─ CLI · Cloud · Languages · SCM
│     System · Web · Music · Personal
├─ Guides
│  ├─ MCP server          <s>was “Advanced”</s>
│  ├─ Desired State Config
│  └─ <i>Authentication</i>       <s>was orphaned</s>
├─ Troubleshooting
│  └─ <s>FAQ split by shell / terminal / editor</s>
└─ Contributing
   ├─ Get started · Add a segment
   ├─ Share a theme
   └─ Contributors</pre>
        <footer><b>Fixes:</b> the wrong landing page, missing indexes, the orphan auth doc, the one-child category, emoji labels, loose root pages. <b>Leaves:</b> the PNG gallery and the text-only segment pages.</footer>
      </article>

      <!-- IA-2 -->
      <article class="ia">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">IA-2 — recommended</p>
          <h3>Four doors</h3>
          <p class="small">Themes and Segments leave <code>/docs</code> and become first-class site sections with their own faceted browsers.</p>
        </header>
<pre class="tree"><b>Nav</b>  Docs · <i>Segments</i> · <i>Themes</i> · Community
     ⌘K · GitHub · <i>Install ▾</i>

<i>/segments</i>            <s>faceted catalog, 117</s>
  search · group · shell · needs auth
  cached · async · has icon
  → links into the docs reference

<i>/themes</i>              <s>faceted gallery, 124</s>
  search · nerd font · powerline
  light/dark · segments used · author
  → <i>/themes/{author}/{name}</i>
  → one-click apply command

<b>/docs</b>
├─ <i>Hub</i>  cards: Install · Configure
│      Reference · Troubleshoot
├─ Start          install → font → shell
│                 → theme → upgrade
├─ Configure      concepts → file → blocks
│                 → segments → colors
│                 → templates → prompts
├─ Reference      <s>machine-generated</s>
│  ├─ Segment reference (117)
│  ├─ Config schema
│  ├─ CLI commands
│  └─ Template functions
├─ Integrate      MCP · DSC · skills · auth
├─ Troubleshoot   by shell · by terminal
│                 by editor · fonts
└─ Contribute

<b>/community</b>       blog · showcase · sponsors
                 swag · Discord</pre>
        <footer><b>Adds:</b> two faceted browsers, per-theme URLs, a docs hub, a Reference tier separate from prose, one honest home for the sponsor/swag/blog cluster currently squatting in primary nav.</footer>
      </article>

      <!-- IA-3 -->
      <article class="ia">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">IA-3</p>
          <h3>Studio-first</h3>
          <p class="small">The configurator becomes the product surface. Docs orbit it. Highest payoff, highest build cost.</p>
        </header>
<pre class="tree"><b>Nav</b>  <i>Studio</i> · Themes · Segments · Docs
     ⌘K · GitHub · Install ▾

<i>/studio</i>             <s>the landing page</s>
